# US-422: real 404s for unknown URLs (fix soft 404).
#
# Cloudflare Pages resolution order: a Pages Function (functions/*) runs first,
# then an exact static-asset match (every prerendered public page —
# /, /pricing, /privacy, /grading/<slug>, … — is a dist/<route>/index.html file
# and is served directly), and only THEN are these _redirects rules evaluated.
#
# IMPORTANT: the client-rendered app shells (/dashboard, /admin, /auth/*,
# /login, /signup, /accept-invite) are NO LONGER served from here. A _redirects
# `→ /index.html 200` rewrite gets canonicalized by Cloudflare Pages into a
# 308 → / (which broke hard-loads / refreshes of every app route). Those
# namespaces are now served as 200 by dedicated Pages Functions
# (functions/dashboard/[[path]].ts, …, functions/_shared/spa-shell.ts) — wired
# in public/_routes.json — which run BEFORE this file. This rule only catches
# paths with NO function and NO static file → a real 404 (no soft-404 indexing).
/*              /404.html     404
